  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Response to Environmental Degradation and Protection of Alternative Energy Sources in Refugee Hosting Communities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Government of Uganda has prioritised a Water/Environment Sector Response Plan to provide the much-needed framework for integrated planning and implementation of environment related activities in refugee-hosting districts.      The Response to Environmental Degradation and Protection of Alternative Energy Sources in Refugee Hosting Communities named &lt;b&gt;the ENAPRO project&lt;/b&gt; has been designed as a direct, fully aligned and explicit development contribution to its implementation.     The overall objective of this project is to increase environmental protection and restoration, to improve sustainable energy for improved livelihoods and rights among displaced populations and their host communities and finally, to improve coordination, planning and capacities on environment and climate change in refugee hosting areas.</narrative>
  </description>
